# Wave W17-V (Route 205): gale turf — wind-valley grass: a lively valley green carrying pale swirl flecks, the valley wind combed into the sward in short strokes (design: honey on the trees, turbines on the hill; the shipped river water, honeytree and flower grass stand byte-preserved and the ground converts around them). Route 205’s own ground — split from Route 201’s lake-shore meadow by the swirl (wind combing vs shore flecks) and from Heritage Forest’s deep shade by value entire: this valley stands in open moving air.
